OL,5,CPIT STRIKEFCoal Board and NUM
OL,6,F may meet on Sunday night......103B203
OL,7,B
OL,8,CTUCFvotes against NEDC boycott.106B206
OL,9,B
OL,10,CDOCKERSFurged to join strike...104B204
OL,12,CRAIL TALKSFend inconclusively,
OL,13,F BR hopes for normal services..115B215
OL,14,B
OL,15,CFOOD POISONINGFHospital death
OL,16,F toll reaches 18...............109B209
OL,18,CSHUTTLEFDiscovery lands safely 114B214
OL,20,CTHE POUNDFfalls to a new low...128
OL,21,B
OL,22,T]F This Ceefax page is fromC05-09-84
OL,23,T]F Much more at: teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11804
SC,0004
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1788570294
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G4/18
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, The Coal Board and the miners' union
OL,6, plan to meet on Sunday night.
OL,7,F
OL,8,FThe new talks were agreed after the
OL,9,FCoal Board wrote to the NUM offering to
OL,10,Fre-open negotiations.
OL,11,F
OL,12,FThe Board's letter apparently refers to
OL,13,Fthe question of whether uneconomic pits
OL,14,Fshould be closed.
OL,16,FIn its reply the NUM says it hopes the
OL,17,Fmeeting will take place - but Mr
OL,18,FScargill has said there is no change in
OL,19,Fthe union's position.
OL,21,F
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]CFrom 05-09-84   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11805
SC,0005
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1788570294
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G5/18
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, The Trades Union Conference voted today
OL,6, not to boycott the National Economic
OL,7, Development Council.
OL,8,F
OL,9,FMr David Basnett, chairman of the TUC
OL,10,FEconomic Committee, in opposing a move
OL,11,Fto pull out of the NEDC, said it was
OL,12,Fnecessary to fight against monetarism
OL,13,Fusing any means possible.
OL,14,F
OL,15,FCongress also approved unanimously a
OL,16,Fmotion condemning the Government's
OL,17,F"damaging" education policy.
OL,18,F
OL,19,FProposed tax reforms were criticised
OL,20,Fand a "fair and equitable system of
OL,21,Fpersonal income tax" called for.
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]CFrom 05-09-84   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11806
SC,0006
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1788570294
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G6/18
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, Transport union leaders have called on
OL,6, all dockers still working to withdraw
OL,7, their labour.
OL,8,F
OL,9,FThe TGWU Docks and Waterways Committee
OL,10,Fhas also asked the union executive to
OL,11,Fcall for the "full physical support" of
OL,12,Fother unions.
OL,14,FThe committee condemned the attempt by
OL,15,Fthe Port of London Authority to hold
OL,16,Fits own ballot of dockers at Tilbury.
OL,18,FIt said such a ballot would provide a
OL,19,Fdistorted response and would probably
OL,20,Flead to similar moves by other port
OL,21,Fauthorities.
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]CFrom 05-09-84   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11807
SC,0007
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1788570294
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G7/18
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, The talks between British Railways and
OL,6, the two main rail unions have ended
OL,7, inconclusively, but BR hopes that next
OL,8, week's disruption can be averted.
OL,9,F
OL,10,FThe unions have planned a work-to-rule
OL,11,Ffrom Monday, followed by a 24-hour
OL,12,Fstrike of rail and tube in the London
OL,13,Farea on Wednesday in protest against
OL,14,Fproposed cuts in jobs.
OL,15,F
OL,16,FUnion leaders said the talks had made
OL,17,Fsome progress and British Rail was
OL,18,Fhopeful that services would be normal
OL,19,Fon Monday. The rail unions report to
OL,20,Ftheir executives on Friday and Mr Jimmy
OL,21,FKnapp of the NUR said the situation was
OL,22,F"delicately poised".
OL,23,                      D]CFrom 05-09-84
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11808
SC,0008
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1788570294
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G8/18
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, The death toll in the food poisoning
OL,6, outbreak at a psychiatric hospital in
OL,7, Wakefield, Yorkshire, has risen to 18.
OL,8,F
OL,9,FThe deaths of seven more patients at
OL,10,Fthe Stanley Royd Hospital were reported
OL,11,Ftoday. Most of the dead were elderly.
OL,12,F
OL,13,FThe outbreak has affected 300 patients
OL,14,Fand several dozen members of staff.
OL,15,F
OL,16,FInquests on 15 victims have been opened
OL,17,Fand adjourned for a fortnight pending
OL,18,Ffurther investigations.
OL,19,F
OL,20,FThe local health authority says the
OL,21,Finfection has passed its peak but the
OL,22,Fexact cause is still not known.
OL,23,F                     D]CFrom 05-09-84
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11809
SC,0009
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1788570294
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G9/18
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, The US space shuttle Discovery has
OL,6, returned safely to earth after a six-
OL,7, day mission.
OL,9,FThe crew of six astronauts made a
OL,10,Fperfect landing at Edwards Air Force
OL,11,Fbase in California at 1338 GMT.
OL,13,FThey successfully launched three
OL,14,Fcommunications satellites during the
OL,15,F2.5 million mile trip.
OL,17,FThe flawless testing of a 10-storey
OL,18,Fsolar sail could lead to the use of the
OL,19,Fconcept for supplying electricity to a
OL,20,Fpermanent US space station. A machine
OL,21,Fto process biological material in space
OL,22,Fwas also tested successfully.
OL,23,F                     D]CFrom 05-09-84
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11810
SC,0010
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1788570294
OL,1,T]W<,,4<,,4<,,4Sp00p000p0p0000p0  C10/18
OL,2,T]W5b(55b(55j5S5 5j -555= 555-4
OL,3,T]W-,,%-,,%-,,%S#!!" #!!!#!##!#!
OL,4,Q]             GEXCHANGES Close
OL,5,F
OL,6,FWidespread switching of funds into the
OL,7,Fdollar dragged other major currencies
OL,8,Ftowards all-time lows. Dealers again
OL,9,Fcited US interest rate trends.
OL,10,F
OL,11,FSterling, whose value in Continental
OL,12,Fterms remained unimpaired despite an
OL,13,Fapparent absence of Bank of England
OL,14,Fsupport, plumbed a new low of $1.2805
OL,15,Fbefore closing at $1.2815, for a loss
OL,16,Fof exactly one cent on the day.
OL,17,F
OL,18,FThe Deutsche Mark, meanwhile, dropped
OL,19,Fto a 13-year low of 2.9550 - and this
OL,20,Fin the face of considerable Bundesbank
OL,21,Fintervention.
OL,22,F
OL,23,Q]GFromC05-09-84G  teletextarchive.com
